t(37, 60, """strategic, in his ancient historical alliance with all the forces of evil in the world .. This alliance will fall completely and be struck with destruction .. This is the sign of the Smoke .. It will destroy all his alliances and make those who allied with him for hundreds of years say to him: everything is over, everything is lost; we and they (the Muslims) are now on an equal footing in strength, so if they are brave and we are cowards, we are finished .. That is why they come to Sham with 960 thousand soldiers, and their commander orders all the ships burned and tells them: either you win or you die .. Even so, this will not change the outcome of their defeat, Allah willing .. The problem with the sign of the Smoke is that it has many consequences .. Unfortunately those who speak about it focus only on its environmental consequences .. its technological consequences .. and its punitive consequences, insisting that it is merely a divine punishment upon the earth to discipline people and make them admit that they erred .. Whereas it is indeed a punishment for the disbelievers and the disobedient among Muslims, no doubt about that, but it also has many strategic dimensions, intertwined and overlapping and not superficial, and it has tremendous, huge political and geopolitical effects during the year, month and week of the Dajjal's rule. When the Dajjal emerges he will present himself as king of the world, claiming "lordship of kingship in the first place, not complete lordship", and he will install himself as ruler of the world, as the hadiths make clear, possessing a state and an army. So the sign of the Smoke is a divine sign, but it has very important political dimensions; it is what will shape the Dajjal's world, which lasts a year, a month and a week. And because of this global political-religious change that will take place over a year, a month and a week, our master Isa, peace be upon him, will descend to end this exceptional global political situation, during which the Romans and the Children of Israel will have reached their full peak and completed their full cycle in rejecting Islam and arrived at the highest rank of rejection, not only by enmity to the true religion but by imposing falsehood with the power of millions of devils who will be summoned for the battle, for the tribulation and for the emergence, something that has never happened before in human history. So the Dajjal's rage at the sign of the Smoke is caused by:
🔴 The anger of his Roman allies at him
🔴 The disappearance of his people's state in the Middle East
🔴 His Roman allies and his people telling him: if you do not come out we will be finished forever and the whole world will be Islamized
🔴 The emergence of a Muslim power (the Islamic world) that will deal with the world with dignity and other things

Finally: from the Dajjal's contempt and disdain for the word (the Smoke) in his dialogue with the Prophet ﷺ I understand the following:
🔴 An attempt to show that he will not be affected, and he is a liar
🔴 The one who shows disdain does so because he is angry, which means that the Prophet ﷺ mentioning the sign in front of him angered him and made him lose his balance, because the mocker is weak; he mocks because he has nothing with which to face the danger except mockery""")

t(37, 1385, """So the matter will be like that in Bayt al-Maqdis for 9 years, or seven or eight; the stronger view in my opinion, and Allah knows best, is that it will be 9 years
So how can one logically and rationally reconcile a hadith graded hasan (sound), which says the Muslims will remain 9 years in whose era the Ummah grows great and the strongest and richest state arises, with the sign of the Smoke having descended on them before that, the sign that reaps the earth clean and makes it as if it had never flourished and returns it to 500 years ago?
The hadith: ("I give you glad tidings of the Mahdi; he is sent among my Ummah at a time of discord among people and earthquakes, and he fills the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and injustice. The dweller of the heaven and the dweller of the earth are pleased with him. He divides wealth sihahan. A man said to him: What is sihahan? He said: Equally among the people. He said: And Allah fills the hearts of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ with contentment, and his justice encompasses them, until he orders a caller to call out: Who has need of wealth? And no one stands up but one man, who says: I do. He says: Go to the keeper, meaning the treasurer, and tell him: the Mahdi orders you to give me wealth. He says to him: Scoop up. Then when he has put it in his lap and brought it out, he regrets it and says: I was the greediest soul in the Ummah of Muhammad; or was what sufficed them not enough for me? He said: So he returns it, but it is not accepted from him, and he is told: We do not take back anything we have given. So it is like that for seven years, or eight years, or nine years; then there is no good in living after him, or he said: then there is no good in life after him").
Summary of the hadith scholar's ruling: its chain of narration is hasan
Narrator: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri""")

t(37, 2165, """The sign of the Smoke and mistaken questions in the comments .. What is the difference between the sign of the Smoke before the Mahdi, which produces a paralysed state with no value, no strength and no industrial resources, and the sign of the Smoke in the last days of the 9 years of his state in Jerusalem, about which it has come that it is a state in which the Ummah grows great as it never did before? What is the difference?
Many do not understand the Mahdi's state. They think the Mahdi's state is an ordinary state. From here, from this gap, their understanding is breached and manipulated. The Mahdi's state resembles no other state in all the human history we know. It is a state with missions, not one mission. Among its missions is to be present, with its leader, for the emergence of the Dajjal, as a mercy from Allah Almighty to this Ummah that the Dajjal emerges while the Mahdi is in it; this is something almost no one I know of reflects upon, and if anyone has reflected on it, well and good. At the time of the Dajjal's emergence the Muslims will need a leadership among them that precedes the Dajjal's appearance, to prepare them for his emergence .. People think the Dajjal is just a hologram in the sky and optical tricks .. People do not truly appreciate what the emergence of the Dajjal means. They do not grasp with us that the whole Ummah will be gathered in Makkah and Madinah in hundreds of millions, not tens of millions, so much so that one of the Mothers of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, asked the Prophet: will Madinah and Makkah have room for all this number? And the Prophet ﷺ said to her: yes. And it is among the proofs of""")

t(38, 60, """his prophethood ﷺ that the number of his Ummah will be huge on that day. So let us ask those who speak morning and evening about the annihilation of the Muslims on that day, and who always love to say to us: the annihilation of the Arabs, the annihilation of the Arabs, the annihilation of the Arabs .. As for Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, about which Arabs did she ask? The Romans were in Sham, Egypt and North Africa, and the Persians were in Iraq in the time of the Prophet ﷺ .. Since the authentic hadith in al-Tirmidhi is about the Arabs, Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, was asking about her own people .. about the Arabs of the Arabian Peninsula, the homeland of the Arabs at that time .. And if those who rush to conclusions, saying the Ummah, Arab and non-Arab, will be annihilated at the time of the Dajjal and most of its sons will have died and perished, were right, then why was Umm Sharik, may Allah be pleased with her, amazed at the numbers? And the Prophet ﷺ confirmed to her that the crowds, vast and great crowds, will flee from the Dajjal to Makkah and Madinah, not a small number, as is clear to every attentive person of sound mind when he reads the hadith "the Arabs on that day are few". The conclusion: the Dajjal emerges in the Mahdi's state, because sheltering these millions in Makkah and Madinah will require a new infrastructure and new structural measures in the environment of the two holy cities, and resources and food for a year, a month and a week so that no famine occurs. So how can all that be prepared with pickaxes, which would need long decades to build an infrastructure holding hundreds of millions, not tens of millions? Indeed, even if it were tens of millions, that is an infrastructure that cannot be attained in 9 or 10 years with the axe and mud!""")

t(38, 825, """The sign of the Smoke and questions in the comments here on the channel
A comment whose author wrote: How can the sign of the Smoke be a punishment and come after the Mahdi; will the Mahdi be punished?
The answer: Understanding becomes difficult when a person does not classify things correctly, on the basis of sound thinking and disciplined understanding! The sign of the Smoke is never a punishment for the Mahdi nor for the believing, monotheist Muslims with him, and this mistaken understanding is what the wrong understanding of the brother, or sister, who wrote the comment is built upon.
The sign of the Smoke is a punishment for the disbelievers and a punishment for the hypocrites among those affiliated with the Muslims at that time. When the Prophet ﷺ spoke to the Dajjal through the body of Ibn Sayyad, he threatened him with the sign of the Smoke and told him that he had hidden it for him. So did the Prophet ﷺ hide something by which his Ummah would be harmed? The answer is no. But for understanding not to fall short, the hadiths must be reflected upon calmly, rationally and with detachment, and the reflection must not be based on championing an opinion; I receive private messages whose authors say: this is how we grew up and lived .. we grew up with the sign of the Smoke being before the Mahdi .. This is the method of championing an opinion, not the method of searching for the truth .. So the matter becomes: it is a cow, but it will fly .. My brother, it is a cow! Never mind, it will fly .. Well, whoever seeks the truth will not fall into this predicament .. The Prophet ﷺ stood one day with the boy Ibn Sayyad before him, in his boyhood, and spoke with the Dajjal through the body of Ibn Sayyad, and the Dajjal answered the Prophet ﷺ through the body of Ibn Sayyad, and the Prophet""")

t(38, 1310, """ﷺ told the Dajjal that he had something hidden for him, and with that hidden thing the Prophet ﷺ was enraging the Dajjal. When the Dajjal felt the rage, he told the Prophet ﷺ that its name was: the Smo .. and he did not complete the word (the Smoke), out of contempt for the sign, belittling it and disdaining it, in disbelief in Allah and lack of reverence for Allah; he did it deliberately, because he is a disbeliever. So the Prophet ﷺ became angry and said to him: Be gone! You will never exceed your measure. For the Prophet ﷺ could not bear that little one mocking one of the signs of Allah, and instead of pronouncing its name in full (the Smoke) saying (the Smo), belittling the sign. So the Prophet ﷺ had the right to be angry, and we all have the right to be angry at such a thing.

The Smoke, then, is what the Prophet ﷺ has hidden for the Dajjal at the end of time. Accordingly, the understanding of some Muslims that the sign is a punishment for the Ummah of Islam is an entirely wrong understanding .. Rather it is the inevitable, decreed sign announcing the end of this world, so that we all meet our Lord .. And there is nothing in it, that is, in the sign, indicating that the Mahdi erred in his rule or that the Muslims with him deviated so that the sign came down to punish them along with the other nations .. All this is caused by the wrong understanding of the meaning of the sign of the Smoke .. which is a torment upon the disbelievers and the ending of a state of the Muslims that will be in Jerusalem for nine years of plenty, wealth, honour and strength, by the text of the hadith with an authentic chain. So how can a hadith with an authentic chain say that the Muslims will be in Jerusalem enjoying, for 9 years, a vast and strong state as the Ummah never enjoyed before, while the sign of the Smoke has already descended on them, the crops have died, the livestock have died, and the hardship that precedes the Dajjal has begun? What kind of reflection is this?

But those who went in an incorrect direction in understanding the sign of the Smoke thought it a punishment upon all the people of the earth .. It is a punishment upon the disbelievers by the text of the Book of Allah, our Great Lord, in which it has come: {"Then watch for the day when the sky brings a visible smoke (10) enveloping the people; this is a painful torment (11) Our Lord, remove the torment from us; we are believers"} The Mahdi and the believers with him, that is, most of the Ummah and not necessarily all of it, do not need to say "we are believers", so the words are on the tongue of the disbelievers, the polytheists and the hypocrites. The matter of the sign of the Smoke will remain stuck in the minds of these brothers and sisters; they will not understand it and will keep saying: no, it is a sign that precedes the Mahdi and it is impossible for it to be after him, because they will keep thinking it is a punishment upon the whole earth, and because they do not connect matters to one another. A statement I heard days ago gave me pause: that the sign of the Smoke must come now because oppression has spread on earth and the people of the earth have deserved the sign!! On what basis does a person decide that the people of the earth have deserved the sign of the Smoke specifically? Why would they not have deserved a swallowing of the earth? Why would they not have deserved the punishment of being stripped of security, plenty, wealth and a comfortable life? All these are punishments, and divine punishments are very many, and Allah Almighty alone is the One who decides which punishment descends on people and on the earth. But for us to assert, speaking in the name of Allah the Great, the King, that what is coming is the sign of the Smoke because the people of the earth have transgressed? Glory be to Allah .. Did Pharaoh not transgress? Did the people of Allah's prophet Nuh, peace be upon him, not transgress? Or did peoples before not transgress greatly? Conceiving of it without asserting it is correct as a method of presentation, but it is wrong as a method of inference! Inferring that humanity has transgressed, so the sign of the Smoke specifically is the sign that must descend!!""")

t(39, 215, """The first universality of Islam took 40 years of effort and toil to be achieved, in a time when a man found no great, ruinous hardship in travelling on horseback for months .. The second universality of Islam, under the pictures in this post, will need 200 years to come about, not just 40 years, because the bodies of people in our time are not accustomed to hardship that people bore 1400 years ago. The pictures in the post show the reality of humanity after the sign of the Smoke! The question: if the second universality of Islam will begin after the sign of the Smoke, as channels say, do the pictures of people's condition in these images help one be convinced that these wretched, hungry people, exposed to a great shock, can spread Islam in the two Americas, in the far east of Asia, in Africa and in Europe?!!""")

